{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs",
  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]/fn[render]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "The agent asks only for outgoing edges and submits without reading\n contents. Its renderer is required by the agent interface, but any\n rendering would imply an unwanted content input. Other agent tests\n exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `fn[render]` in `impl[Render/AgentInputRenderer<GraphWithChangingEdges>]` inside `fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` is valid.\n\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced commentary block on an explicit function with a body, which is a permitted target. The reason is written as fenced citation commentary, so it counts as a tracked justification.\n- **Substance:** The reason is not just difficulty. `render` is a panic guard. The test checks that an edge-only conversation never renders node contents, so reaching `render` would mean the test had already failed. The renderer is still required to build the `Validator` with `.with_agent(&agent, &agent.renderer)`.\n- **Agreement with the source:** I read `Ask::execute` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs`. It calls `renderer.render` only for nodes produced by explicit insertions (`Insertion::Current` or `Insertion::Successors`). The test calls `ctx.ask::<bool>()` with no insertions, so `render` is never reached. The tool-session `dispatch` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs` also renders only when the agent requests contents. This test's script requests `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`, so it never reads contents.\n- **Other tests:** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` has other renderers, `Renderer` and `DistinctPages`. They return node contents, which fits the claim that other tests exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents.\n\nI found no gap.",
